ll versions after 4.5 beta 3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.rc1 - Linux Mint 22.1 (Xia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (nvidia; 570.169) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.24 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a font variation, with a negative glyth extra spacing number, the minimum size for a label (or rich text label), becomes smaller than the actual font rendered, causing many layout bugs, when trying to update my game to the latest version, wheras in 4.5 beta 3, it was working as expected (I use the extra spacing for a bitmap font, but also applies to standard fonts too)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1.  Create a variation font, and set it to be used on a text label\n2. Set the variation fonts \"Extra Spacing\" value for glyth, to be a negative number (-8 is the best)\n3. See how the minimum size is smaller, than the actual text rendered, causing text to be rendered outside the boundary\n\n<img width=\"454\" height=\"240\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b6d05904-5b95-4542-9c6d-757a20c0c385\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[FontTest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22194601/FontTest.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.